          <div  class="title-page">
               <p>(E) <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">Normal Operation Procedure:</b></p>
              <table cellpadding="2">
                
    <tr>
         <th style="width:6%;">Sr. No.</th>
            <th style="width:68%;">Operation Procedure</th>
            <th style="width:11%;">Action by</th>
            <th style="width:10%;">Check</th>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>1</td>
        <td>
            Ensure compliance with MGL Life Saving Rules and COP requirements.
            Conduct site specific HIRA.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>2</td>
        <td>
            Inform Emergency control room about commencement of NRO.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>3</td>
        <td>
            Issue work permit for confined space entry for entering steel valve
            chambers.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>4</td>
        <td>
           Close the valve V03 (Size 6”) &amp; V04 (Size 6”) completely and all allow all CNG Stations mentioned in Annexure-I to consume the line pack and trip at low suction pressure. Then allow the DRS 32, DRS 33 &amp; DRS 40 to run till 6 Bar inlet pressure and then close both stream inlet valve of DRS 32, DRS 33 &amp; DRS 40
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>5</td>
        <td>
            Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of valve V13 (Size 3/4”), V20 (Size 3/4”), V29 (Size 3/4”) &amp; V35 (Size 3/4”)  and remove if found.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>6</td>
        <td>
            Connect vent stack and flame arrestor at Valve V13, V20, V29 &amp; V35. Open Valve V13, V20, V29 &amp; V35 and vent the residual gas in the pipeline using a vent stack and flame arrestor.<b> Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3- Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>7</td>
        <td>
       Close Valve V09, V21. Also, Close Valve V29 &amp; put blind flange.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>8</td>
        <td>
           Disconnect the suction inlet flange of all CNG stations (mentioned in Annexure-I) compressors and positive isolation to be done.
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>9</td>
        <td>
            Issue Testing, Commissioning and Purging permit. Connect the Nitrogen hose at Valve V22 and start Nitrogen purging from valve V13, V20 &amp; V35 using a vent stack and flame arrestor.<b> Refer: PTW System’</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>10</td>
        <td>
            Check % of gas at Valve V13, V20 &amp; V35 and stop nitrogen purging when the level falls below the safe limit (Ensure – 0PPM)<b> Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3- Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>11</td>
        <td>
            Issue hot and cold work permit, allow the construction team to cut the pipe at point ‘A’ &amp; point ‘B’ for Hook up of newly laid 6” NB Steel pipeline between point A &amp; B. Also, Issue Hot work and cold work permit allow construction team to cut the pipe at Point ‘C’ , ‘D’ &amp; ‘E’ for replacement of existing valve assembly with newly fabricated (duly tested) valve assembly. (Cutting to be done from Hacksaw)<b>Refer: PTW System</b>
        </td>
        <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>

    <tr>
        <td>12</td>
        <td>
            Complete the Connectivity at Point A &amp; Point B with Existing
            Pipeline &amp; Newly laid pipeline.Also, complete the connectivity at Point ‘C’ , ‘D’ &amp; ‘E’ and replace valve assembly.
        </td>
        <td>Contractor Team</td>
        <td></td>
    </tr>
      <tr>
            <td>13</td>
            <td>
                Ensure quality of joints by reviewing NDT reports of the welds.
                <b> Refer COP: Section 52 (Clause No. 8 - NDT)</b>
            </td>
            <td>
                O&amp;M Engineer &amp;<br/>
                MGL QA Engineer &amp;<br/>
                NDT Agency
            </td>
          <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>14</td>
            <td>
               Open Valve V09 &amp; V21 completely. Close Check for any potential sources of ignition around valve V13, V20, V35, inlet vent of DRS 32 , inlet vent of DRS 33 &amp; Inlet vent of DRS 40 and remove if any before venting. Also, Close Valve V22 and put blind flange. 
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td >15</td>
            <td >
                Issue Charging and commissioning permit and then open Valve V03 slowly and start venting from Valve V13, V20, V35, Inlet vent DRS 32, Inlet vent of DRS 33, &amp; inlet vent of DRS 40 by using vent stack and flame arrestor. <b>(Refer: PTW System)</b>
            </td>
            <td >O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td ></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td >16</td>
            <td >
                Continue venting till 95% GIA is achieved at Valve V13, V20, V35, Inlet vent DRS 32, Inlet vent of DRS 33, &amp; inlet vent of DRS 40 and then close valve V13, V20, V35 and put blind flange. Then open Valve V04. Also, check 95% GIA is achieved at the inlet of all CNG stations mentioned in Annexure-I. Re-connect compressor suction inlet flange of at all CNG stations mentioned in Annexure-I and then open Compressors inlet valve and restart compressors <b>(Refer: WI: O &amp; M WI 102)</b>
            </td>
            <td >O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td ></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>17</td>
            <td>
                Open inlet valve of DRS 32, DRS 33 &amp; DRS 40 both stream &amp; take DRS 32, DRS 33 &amp; DRS 40 online. (Refer: WI: O &amp; M WI 110)
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>18</td>
            <td>
           Check 95% GIA at inlet vent valve at Trident MRS. Then take Trident MRS online.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Engineer/Technician</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>19</td>
            <td>
                Check all flanged joint for leakages with soap solution &amp; Gascoseeker.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Technician</td><td></td>
        </tr>

        <tr>
            <td>20</td>
            <td>
                Close all work permits and Inform Emergency control room about the completion of NRO.
            </td>
            <td>O&amp;M Engineer</td>
            <td></td>
        </tr>

</table>
