               <p> <b style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000; font-weight: bold;">(G) Contingency Action Plan:</b></p>
            
                 
             <p><b style="text-decoration:underline;color:red"> In case of Passing of Valve V04:</b> </p>
 <table>	
        <tr>
            <th>Sr. No.</th>
            <th>Description of work</th>
            <th>Responsibility</th>
        </tr>
     <tr><td rowspan="3" style="background-color:gray;"><b>Action Steps in case f Contingency</b></td></tr>
        <tr><td>1</td><td> Give information to the Emergency control room about the Passing of Valve V04.</td><td >O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>2</td><td> Inform CNG stations regarding shutdown as <b>per Annexure - IV</b></td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
		<tr><td>3</td><td>Check for any potential sources of ignition in the vicinity of valve V08 (Size 2”) and remove if found. </td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>4</td><td> Close valve V02 &amp; open valve V07</td><td>O&amp;M Technician </td></tr>
     <tr><td>5</td><td>Connect vent stack and flame arrestor at Valve V08. Open Valve V08 and vent the residual gas in the pipeline using a vent stack and flame arrestor. If still gas is found passing, then abandon the NRO and inform the emergency control room. <b>Refer COP: Section 08 (Clause no. 3- Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b> </td><td>O&amp;M Technician &amp; O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>6</td><td>If gas is not passing then carry out the work as per the normal operation procedure, ensuring pre and post purging as per the sections isolated in conformance with COP <b>Section 08 (Clause no. 3- Purging &amp; commissioning of mains)</b> </td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>7</td><td> Restore the valves to its original positions that are prior to the start of the NRO. </td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
     <tr><td>8</td><td> Inform Emergency control Room about completion of NRO.</td><td>O&amp;M Engineer </td></tr>
        </table> 
             
